          "Sampling error, coder disagreement, and records that never reached the system each cap what the number can claim. Publish the overlap agreement and any disputed code rather than declaring the coding clean. One unit and one window produced this number, so it cannot stand in for an industry benchmark. The closing paragraph states what the review still cannot see.",
          "A finished file does not prove the coverage call was right, because this review scores documentation rather than claim quality. The design cannot read intent and cannot describe a claim that left no trace in any system. Put the caveats directly under the finding so a reader cannot lift the number without them. If the rule changes midstream, keep the earlier and later versions and tag each claim."
